From b42e2eb8f02a747e24fac01c966a987258538553 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:08:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/57] hw/sensor, hw/arm: Thermo 8 Click (MCP9808) on the MC00
 board headers

The PIC32CM MC00 Curiosity Pro takes MikroElektronika Click boards on
EXT1/EXT2. Machine options ext1=<click> and ext2=<click> plug one in:
its I2C target goes on SERCOM2's bus and its INT output on the header's
pin 9 (PB02 on EXT1, PA28 on EXT2); the device is /machine/extN-click.

First Click: thermo8, an MCP9808 temperature sensor (mchp-mcp9808, data
sheet DS25095) at 0x18. Register pointer, CONFIG, TUPPER/TLOWER/TCRIT,
TA with its limit flags and resolution, IDs, shutdown, the limit locks,
and the open-drain ALERT in comparator, interrupt and critical-only
modes. The "temperature" property (milli-degrees C) sets the reading,
also at run time. Modelled from the data sheet; no physical Click has
been checked.

PORT gains "pa-levels"/"pb-levels": every pad's level, external
drivers and pulls included, so a board view can show signals the chip
does not drive.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
